--- !u!114 &826226674
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 826226669}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: c3e757e2d127424418697c7f630eae63, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Tutorial
  tutorialSteps:
  - Welcome to Level 2, the Coastal Reef. Water tiles block your ground towers, and
    enemy threats intensify. Watch out for Plastic Bombers entering the battlefield.
    They explode on impact, dealing heavy area-of-effect damage to your defenses.
  - The pollution is intensifying on the shores. Build a Crystal Spring tower near
    the path. It sprays pure water to activate an AoE Slow mechanic, slowing down
    fast-moving toxic groups and giving your defensive units more time to strike.
  - The enemy forces are pushing harder. Beware of Oil Lighters entering the fray.
    They will set active pollution puddles on fire, creating dangerous hazards that
    deal heavy damage-over-time to any units caught in the blaze.
  - The enemy density is reaching its peak as we prepare for the final sector push.
    Ensure your frontline layout is secure. Use your Forest Knights to hold the path
    choke points and position your Greenshot towers to cover the winding shoreline.
  - Warning. The final wave of this biome is here and the Oil Behemoth boss has arrived.
    This massive ground threat leaves a sticky oil trail that accelerates enemy movement
    and explodes with massive area damage upon death. Concentrate all your fire to
    bring it down.
  - Do not give up ground to the corruption. You must use your Cleanse mechanics
    to reduce the overall pollution levels before they max out. Keep the contamination
    meter down at all costs, or it is Game Over.
  tutorialImages:
  - {fileID: 1596308837}
  tutorialTMPText: {fileID: 140925531}
  nextButton: {fileID: 0}
  prevButton: {fileID: 0}
  closeButton: {fileID: 0}
  tutorialCanvasGroup: {fileID: 826226673}
